			},
			"date": "2024-07-05T15:09:31.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Wait, how can this ever work? Doesn't that resolve to different fonts depending on browser, OS etc?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112734516625600748",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriskirknielsen/112734516563325007",
			"author": {
				"name": "Christopher Kirk-Nielsen",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriskirknielsen",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/112/011/424/167/261/417/original/b7483cef1bc6d1dd.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-05T15:10:08.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yes, but counterpoint: how else would I know my CSS it totally borked?</p><p>(I actually have noticed a font failing to load thanks to this in a recent project, so I'm only half joking)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112734520291713930",
			"parentId": "112734510543721196",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112734520291713930",
