		},
		{
			"id": "112734579293253283",
			"parentId": "112734506741274468",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@blogdiva/112734579183119847",
			"author": {
				"name": "your auntifa liza 🇵🇷  🦛 🦦",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@blogdiva",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/649/552/828/625/044/original/97dd263dd469a515.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-05T15:26:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p>why is this necessary? </p><p>been developing with web techs since the 1990s (yes, literally since i got hold of Mosaic sometime in 1994-1995) because am dyslexic and have spent an inordinate amount of decades finding the right combination of fonts and css to attend to my dyslexia needs. </p><p>i wouldn't care from that perspective given i change all my browsers and create very intentional CSS themes for my web projects, but it would irritate me with the random browser i couldn't control</p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112734585738504423",
			"parentId": "112734520291713930",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@rauschma/112734585653509270",
