				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/291/906/591/238/009/original/76fd351b6f7a848e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-05T15:27:42.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Genuinely curious where things will go in the future—ATM sans-serif fonts still dominate user interfaces.</p><p>I personally like Palatino: <a href=\"https://exploringjs.com/js/book/ch_new-javascript-features.html#ch_new-javascript-features\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">exploringjs.com/js/book/ch_new</span><span class=\"invisible\">-javascript-features.html#ch_new-javascript-features</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
