			},
			"date": "2024-07-05T15:38:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I have my default browser set to comic sans as a way of noticing if I’ve accidentally left something on the page unstyled. Always amusing when you double take on a big famous website with some comic sans.</p><p>All of which to say, changing to a sans fonts in general I’m fine with, but sans-serif itself seems a little not-fun-enough, don’t you think?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
