			"date": "2024-07-05T16:44:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span><br>“Serif fonts for coding” by <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://bright.rosy-colored.space/@george\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>george</span></a></span><br><a href=\"https://www.georgeho.org/fonts-for-coding/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">georgeho.org/fonts-for-coding/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p><p>– Could also work as a coding font: <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Courier+Prime\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">fonts.google.com/specimen/Cour</span><span class=\"invisible\">ier+Prime</span></a><br>– Interestingly, even sans-serif coding fonts tend to add serifs to (e.g.): 1, I, l</p>",
